92186348052 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j,k}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bed05d64-8314-58af-9149-10494ba514ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j,k}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77990" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/20/20aff9b0dd1ea6aaab8cfa932317e83015956ac355349d5ae3d744de289bdae5.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e54521b0-9af8-56df-9ce1-bb0fae27ed61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1074 "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-43892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that ${i,j}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ and that the images of $i$ and $j$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨1,4⟩$ and $⟨5,-1⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3dc8d6e7-0a45-5ad2-ab8b-ad2aa66146a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392561 #edb/ref 1074 "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for this linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392562 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3447986d-3f82-5757-965c-a7760fd57f01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392563 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392563 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392563 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15ba0435-b153-5558-8f5a-925432a2b387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392564 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392564 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392564 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e05dbfc-ecf4-58c3-b969-07ec7346d204" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392565 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392565 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392565 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd47cfc2-c2e7-5ddf-829a-e85a70e1f5cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392566 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392